From: turbo-boo <59400127+turbo-boo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Drop incompatible recorder cache for Cinematic

The recorder singleton can contain a pre-created ordinary video recorder when
CinematicModule is constructed. Reusing that controller blocks in reset before
the Cinematic recorder is created, leaving camera setup permanently switching
with controls disabled.

Discard the cached controller only for an actual CinematicModule instance.
Other video modes retain the stock pre-create path.
---
 smali_classes2/com/android/camera/module/VideoModule.smali | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/smali_classes2/com/android/camera/module/VideoModule.smali b/smali_classes2/com/android/camera/module/VideoModule.smali
index 03225356..05a1ce56 100644
--- a/smali_classes2/com/android/camera/module/VideoModule.smali
+++ b/smali_classes2/com/android/camera/module/VideoModule.smali
@@ -160,6 +160,16 @@
 
     move-result-object v1
 
+    instance-of v2, p0, Lcom/android/camera/features/mode/cinematic/CinematicModule;
+
+    if-eqz v2, :cinematic_cache_ready
+
+    const/4 v2, 0x0
+
+    invoke-virtual {v1, v2}, Lcom/android/camera/module/video/t;->b(I)V
+
+    :cinematic_cache_ready
+
     iget-object v2, v1, Lcom/android/camera/module/video/t;->b:Ljava/lang/Object;
 
     monitor-enter v2
-- 
2.43.0
